\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Lumped-parameter mechatronic model of the lithography step-and-scan tool, following \cite  {Al-Rawashdeh2022_Caracterization}. The dashed vertical line is the intended trajectory $P_d$. Each stage block is offset from $P_d$ by its generalised in-plane displacement $f_{i,j}$ (blue double-headed arrows). Horizontal Kelvin--Voigt elements $(K_{i,j},\,C_{i,j})$ couple each scanning stage laterally to the fixed structural reference. Vertical elements $(K_1,C_1)$ and $(K_2,C_2)$ provide passive vibration isolation between the floor $\mathcal  {F}_0$ and the base frame $\mathcal  {F}_1$, and between $\mathcal  {F}_1$ and the metrology frame $\mathcal  {F}_2$ that holds the projection lens.}}{1}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:litho_model_final}{{1}{1}{}{figure.1}{}}
